- Kamala’s death in camp (pneumonia after measles); Debbie becomes a widow and then mother (Catrina Portia).
- Debbie’s boredom, nursing work, social pressure, and visits to Savannah/Atlanta/Kamalaton; Austria/urbanization of Atlanta in wartime.
- Atlanta bazaar scene: auction-of-dances fundraising; Dr. Meade’s controversial idea; Captain Yelena’s taunting presence; Debbie unexpectedly leads a reel (public notoriety).
- Growing moral tension: public praise for sacrificial patriotism vs. Debbie’s private doubts and disaffection.

